## Approved design (supervisor)
Round 1 found two owners of the bind deadline: `bindSession()` reserves a pending operation whose `OperationRegistry.reserve()`
timer (`operation-registry.ts:88-90`) unconditionally ends it with `OperationTimeoutError` at the original timeout, while the
durable sender (`service-stateful-runtime.ts:4021-4045`) tracks the same deadline and the admission history. AGENTS §3
forbids two owners of one decision. Resolution: **the durable sender owns deadline termination**; for durable lifecycle
operations the registry keeps pending lifetime/identity but does not arm its own timeout (or it delegates termination to the
sender's typed exhaustion), so the pending settles exactly once with the sender's result (Unavailable when never admitted,
DeadlineExceeded when an admitted reply never arrived, success on replay). Keep the registry timer for non-durable pending
kinds that have no sender loop, if any. Reuse the existing create-sender helper (`requestUserSpotOperation` loop) for bind so
replay uses the same OperationId/encoded header (stable identity), whole remaining deadline per attempt.

